{
  "summary": "Verify final scripts and witnesses in FinalizePSBT using PSBTInputSignedAndVerified rather than trusting existing final fields. This prevents finalizepsbt from marking a transaction as complete when it contains invalid final script data.",
  "problem": "When a PSBT input with a non-witness UTXO already contains final scriptSig or scriptWitness fields, ProduceSignature exits early and FinalizePSBT treats the input as complete without verifying the script. As a result, finalizepsbt returns complete: true and produces a raw transaction hex that mempool validation rejects, contradicting analyzepsbt.",
  "evidence": [
    "Author provides a concrete reproduction: taking a signed P2WPKH PSBT with a non_witness_utxo and flipping one bit in the final witness causes finalizepsbt to output complete: true, whereas testmempoolaccept rejects the resulting hex with mempool-script-verify-flag-failed.",
    "Follows merged PR #30357 and PR #33014, which fixed the exact same unverified final script issue in FillPSBT and descriptorprocesspsbt."
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "Small fix (+31/-1) accompanied by a regression test in test/functional/rpc_psbt.py.",
  "changed_since_previous": "",
  "card": "FinalizePSBT is updated to verify existing final scriptSig and scriptWitness data using PSBTInputSignedAndVerified before declaring an input complete. Today, finalizepsbt trusts existing final script fields without verification on inputs with a non_witness_utxo, leading to cases where it returns complete: true along with an invalid raw transaction hex that fails mempool acceptance. This aligns FinalizePSBT with prior fixes in FillPSBT (#30357) and descriptorprocesspsbt (#33014). One behavioral change is that final scripts that are valid by consensus but non-standard will now return complete: false.",
  "needs": ["diff"],
  "confidence": "high",
  "uncertainties": [],
  "risk": {
    "level": "medium",
    "touches": ["rpc_api"],
    "why": "A flaw in final script verification could cause finalizepsbt to reject valid PSBTs or produce malformed transactions during finalization."
  }
}
